Subject: [PATCH] sidebar: the side panel can open on the other side of the page

The engine places the sidebar panel (#sidebar-box: the assistant, the
bookmarks, the history, any extension's sidebar) on the same side as the
launcher and the vertical tabs. SidebarController.setPosition() gives each
child of #browser a flex order: the DOM order, or its reverse when
sidebar.position_start is false, so the launcher, the tabs and the panel
always move together.

With nulavio.sidebar.panelOpposite true (a setting in Aparência, off by
default), setPosition() then gives the panel and its splitter the orders
past the page on the other side: after it when the tabs are on the left,
before it when they are on the right. The launcher and the tabs stay where
they are. The panel's splitter resolves its sibling in DOM order and its
side in order order (nsSplitterFrame), as with position_start false, so it
still resizes the panel. The root gets nulavio-panel-opposite, which
Nulavio's own sheets read for the margins (horizon.css, window-band.css).
A lazy preference getter calls setPosition() again when the setting
changes, as the engine's own getter does for sidebar.position_start.

Why a patch: the same two orders set from outside (a MutationObserver
in a Shell module) would be undone on each setPosition() and redone a frame
later, and would stop silently if a release orders #browser another way;
the patch stops the build instead (#249, #242,
docs/research/assistant-opposite-side.md). Off, nothing changes.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not proposed (a Nulavio layout option; #527).
---
--- a/browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js
+++ b/browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js
@@ -1021,6 +1021,18 @@
     [...browser.children].forEach((node, i, children) => {
       node.style.order = this._positionStart ? i + 1 : children.length - i;
     });
+    // Nulavio (#249, #527): the panel and its splitter on the other side of
+    // the page, while the launcher and the vertical tabs stay where they are.
+    const panelOpposite = this._nulavioPanelOpposite;
+    if (panelOpposite) {
+      const last = browser.children.length + 1;
+      this._splitter.style.order = this._positionStart ? last - 1 : 1;
+      this._box.style.order = this._positionStart ? last : 0;
+    }
+    document.documentElement.toggleAttribute(
+      "nulavio-panel-opposite",
+      panelOpposite
+    );
     let sidebarContainer = document.getElementById("sidebar-container");
     let sidebarMain = document.querySelector("sidebar-main");
 
@@ -2808,6 +2820,24 @@
       SidebarController._maybeAnimate(() => {
         SidebarController.setPosition();
       });
+    }
+  }
+);
+// Nulavio (#527): the panel's side, read by setPosition() and applied again
+// when the setting changes.
+XPCOMUtils.defineLazyPreferenceGetter(
+  SidebarController,
+  "_nulavioPanelOpposite",
+  "nulavio.sidebar.panelOpposite",
+  false,
+  () => {
+    if (
+      !SidebarController.uninitializing &&
+      !SidebarController.inSingleTabWindow
+    ) {
+      SidebarController._maybeAnimate(() => {
+        SidebarController.setPosition();
+      });
     }
   }
 );
